1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:02,252
[theme song playing]

2
00:00:02,253 --> 00:00:04,421
<i>♪ You, just us ♪</i>

3
00:00:04,422 --> 00:00:08,133
<i>♪ Just this, just 'cause ♪</i>

4
00:00:08,134 --> 00:00:09,593
<i>♪ Just because ♪</i>

5
00:00:10,678 --> 00:00:13,723
<i>♪ When you say my name, it's different ♪</i>

6
00:00:15,641 --> 00:00:17,726
<i>♪ Just because ♪</i>

7
00:00:17,727 --> 00:00:23,189
<i>♪ Every little second feels infinite ♪</i>

8
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:25,025
<i>♪ No lie, no reason ♪</i>

9
00:00:26,444 --> 00:00:28,446
<i>♪ No fair design ♪</i>

10
00:00:31,115 --> 00:00:34,451
<i>♪ I'm yours ♪</i>

11
00:00:34,452 --> 00:00:37,412
<i>♪ Just because ♪</i>

12
00:00:37,413 --> 00:00:39,957
<i>♪ Mm, just because ♪</i>

13
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:42,959
This drama is a work of fiction.

14
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,377
The characters, events,
place names, organizations,

15
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:45,754
and other elements depicted
are unrelated to reality.

16
00:00:45,755 --> 00:00:46,963
Some images and audio were created
using generative AI technology.

17
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:49,216
[up-tempo music playing]

18
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:51,677
[siren wailing in distance]

19
00:01:00,561 --> 00:01:02,313
[electricity buzzing]

20
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,278
[car lock beeps]

21
00:01:15,785 --> 00:01:16,827
[screaming]

22
00:01:17,411 --> 00:01:19,371
[smoke alarm blaring]

23
00:01:22,958 --> 00:01:25,336
[engine revving]

24
00:01:27,963 --> 00:01:31,716
CAR EXPLODES AFTER SWITCHING ON ENGINE
IN UNDERGROUND PARKING LOT

25
00:01:31,717 --> 00:01:34,052
EPISODE 1

26
00:01:34,053 --> 00:01:35,930
[upbeat music playing]

27
00:01:39,975 --> 00:01:41,893
[line ringing]

28
00:01:41,894 --> 00:01:44,354
This is Kang Yi-ji
from Chronic Motors' Legal Affairs.

29
00:01:44,355 --> 00:01:45,271
TECHNICAL INVESTIGATION TEAM
KIM MIN-SEOP

30
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:48,399
I'm calling to check on the progress of
the investigation into the vehicle fire.

31
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,193
INCOMING CALL
LEGAL AFFAIRS INTERN IM EUN-HA

32
00:01:50,194 --> 00:01:51,110
[phone beeping]

33
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:53,404
Uh... I'm sorry.
I'm going to have to call you back.

34
00:01:53,405 --> 00:01:54,782
[engine revving]

35
00:01:56,367 --> 00:01:57,826
[Eun-ha] Where are you, Ms. Kang?

36
00:01:57,827 --> 00:02:00,328
Mr. Jung from Team 2
took the files on the car fire.

37
00:02:00,329 --> 00:02:03,791
The CEO says Team 2 will take over
and proceed with the settlement.

38
00:02:04,667 --> 00:02:07,669
Settlement? I'm headed
to the hospital to meet the victim.

39
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:11,923
Uh, well... It's because the car owner's
post online brought a flood of articles.

40
00:02:11,924 --> 00:02:13,174
<i>I'll send it to you first.</i>

41
00:02:13,175 --> 00:02:15,511
[upbeat music continues]

42
00:02:20,432 --> 00:02:21,892
[tires screeching]

43
00:02:27,523 --> 00:02:30,025
- [tires screeching]
- [car horn honking]

44
00:02:39,201 --> 00:02:40,077
[man] Get out.

45
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:43,539
[woman grunting]

46
00:02:45,666 --> 00:02:47,625
[woman shudders] I told you,

47
00:02:47,626 --> 00:02:50,545
I have nothing more to say to you.

48
00:02:50,546 --> 00:02:53,089
Talk to me.
What's wrong this time? I'll help you.

49
00:02:53,090 --> 00:02:55,550
[woman] I don't know. Just stop this!

50
00:02:55,551 --> 00:02:57,928
- You can't be serious!
- [woman grunts]

51
00:03:02,975 --> 00:03:05,059
- This one.
- Sure, just one moment, please.

52
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:06,729
[cell phone vibrates]

53
00:03:09,023 --> 00:03:09,856
KIM DONG-SEOK

54
00:03:09,857 --> 00:03:12,151
HAVE YOU EATEN?
CAN WE TALK AFTER WORK?

55
00:03:13,152 --> 00:03:14,944
PLEASE ADVISE ON THE DRAFT PRESS RELEASE

56
00:03:14,945 --> 00:03:16,989
- [vendor] Here you are, enjoy!
- Ah!

57
00:03:17,573 --> 00:03:18,740
- Take care.
- Thanks.

58
00:03:18,741 --> 00:03:22,077
Hey! Let's just talk! Okay? Park Mi-jin!

59
00:03:22,703 --> 00:03:24,872
- [Mi-jin screams]
- [man exclaims]

60
00:03:27,249 --> 00:03:29,667
[Mi-jin] Damn it! Please don't follow me.

61
00:03:29,668 --> 00:03:31,085
[sighs] Just let me go.

62
00:03:31,086 --> 00:03:32,962
Running away won't solve anything!

63
00:03:32,963 --> 00:03:34,339
Did I do something wrong?

64
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:36,925
I'm going to study abroad.
You and I are over.

65
00:03:36,926 --> 00:03:40,345
[man] We've been doing well for a year.
Why are you doing this out of nowhere?

66
00:03:40,346 --> 00:03:41,721
[sighs in exasperation]

67
00:03:41,722 --> 00:03:43,389
Pay for the damage.

68
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:44,974
[scoffs] Stay out of this.

69
00:03:44,975 --> 00:03:46,726
Well, I'm the victim here.

70
00:03:46,727 --> 00:03:49,145
You know causing
a disturbance in public like this

71
00:03:49,146 --> 00:03:51,189
and damaging someone else's property
are criminal offenses, right?

72
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:52,273
[scoffs] What?

73
00:03:52,274 --> 00:03:55,568
Also following and threatening
someone like this is a crime.

74
00:03:55,569 --> 00:03:56,945
It's considered stalking.

75
00:03:56,946 --> 00:04:00,490
Up to three years in prison,
or a fine of up to 30 million won.

76
00:04:00,491 --> 00:04:01,742
[sighs] Look, we're...

77
00:04:02,451 --> 00:04:03,786
Hey! Hey, hey! Park Mi...

78
00:04:04,828 --> 00:04:06,788
Hey, who do you think you are, huh?

79
00:04:06,789 --> 00:04:09,124
I already told you. I'm the victim here.

80
00:04:12,044 --> 00:04:13,212
[man sighs]

81
00:04:15,673 --> 00:04:17,548
I'll give this back
when you buy me a new one.

82
00:04:17,549 --> 00:04:18,926
[sighs heavily]

83
00:04:25,975 --> 00:04:28,435
There's no point holding on
to someone who's emotionally left.

84
00:04:29,019 --> 00:04:30,645
Think whatever you want.

85
00:04:30,646 --> 00:04:32,939
Anyway, the fruit is yours now,
so take it.

86
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:35,442
Don't throw it away.
That would be a total waste.

87
00:04:35,985 --> 00:04:38,195
Uh... [scoffs]

88
00:04:39,405 --> 00:04:41,906
Yeah, I'll get right on that. [grunts]

89
00:04:41,907 --> 00:04:44,492
HANKOOK UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

90
00:04:44,493 --> 00:04:45,619
[knock on door]

91
00:04:50,082 --> 00:04:54,210
[sighs] Hello. I'm Kang Yi-ji
from Chronic Motors' Legal Affairs.

92
00:04:54,211 --> 00:04:55,546
[sighs]

93
00:04:58,549 --> 00:05:00,091
How are you feeling now?

94
00:05:00,092 --> 00:05:02,343
We're very sorry this happened to you.

95
00:05:02,344 --> 00:05:04,303
However,
our specialized investigation team

96
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,348
will determine the cause of the fire.

97
00:05:06,849 --> 00:05:08,558
What do you mean, "cause"?

98
00:05:08,559 --> 00:05:11,853
I nearly died getting
in your company's car! You got that?

99
00:05:11,854 --> 00:05:15,023
With this scar on my arm,
I can't even wear short sleeves anymore.

100
00:05:15,024 --> 00:05:17,066
Yes, I understand completely.

101
00:05:17,067 --> 00:05:19,610
But we need to establish
the accurate cause first

102
00:05:19,611 --> 00:05:22,030
- before we can determine compensation.
- [sighs]

103
00:05:22,031 --> 00:05:25,742
When was your last time you brought
your car in for a service inspection?

104
00:05:25,743 --> 00:05:27,535
I don't know, my husband handles that.

105
00:05:27,536 --> 00:05:28,870
Then have you had the audio system

106
00:05:28,871 --> 00:05:31,664
or any other interior equipment
modified by a third party?

107
00:05:31,665 --> 00:05:32,875
Not a chance.

108
00:05:34,376 --> 00:05:36,169
Then during the last heavy rain,

109
00:05:36,170 --> 00:05:38,129
could your car have been
exposed to a flooded area?

110
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:39,213
Who even cares?

111
00:05:39,214 --> 00:05:43,718
Ah, our vehicles are constructed in a way
so that spontaneous fires are unlikely,

112
00:05:43,719 --> 00:05:45,136
- so we have to find a cause.
- I see.

113
00:05:45,137 --> 00:05:47,680
You're blaming us for the fire
based on our maintenance history?

114
00:05:47,681 --> 00:05:49,891
I'm not trying
to determine who's at fault.

115
00:05:49,892 --> 00:05:51,726
Do cars catch fire
when they get rained on?

116
00:05:51,727 --> 00:05:52,685
No, they don't!

117
00:05:52,686 --> 00:05:54,271
Why did this only happen to us, huh?

118
00:05:55,481 --> 00:05:57,315
I understand how upsetting this is.

119
00:05:57,316 --> 00:06:00,985
But we need to rule out every possible
theory in order to solve the problem.

120
00:06:00,986 --> 00:06:03,571
And this process
is essential for you as well.

121
00:06:03,572 --> 00:06:05,448
[sighs] Okay, fine.

122
00:06:05,449 --> 00:06:08,410
Our apartment complex has
never suffered any flood damage.

123
00:06:13,165 --> 00:06:14,249
[Yi-ji grunts]

124
00:06:14,833 --> 00:06:16,293
[cell phone vibrating]

125
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:22,673
MOM

126
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:25,051
[cell phone continues vibrating]

127
00:06:25,052 --> 00:06:26,386
[sighs]

128
00:06:30,307 --> 00:06:31,475
MISSED CALL MOM
MESSAGE

129
00:06:34,645 --> 00:06:36,479
[Kyung-shim] <i>Dong-seok came by yesterday</i>

130
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:39,440
<i>and fixed the broken faucet
and changed the light bulbs.</i>

131
00:06:39,441 --> 00:06:43,027
<i>He's so thorough and reliable
that I think he's a keeper.</i>

132
00:06:43,028 --> 00:06:47,323
<i>Trust your mom
and keep seeing him this time, okay?</i>

133
00:06:47,324 --> 00:06:48,951
[Yi-ji sighs]

134
00:06:50,369 --> 00:06:51,494
[cell phone vibrating]

135
00:06:51,495 --> 00:06:53,579
<i>You don't need to see someone
for too long.</i>

136
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:57,084
<i>Anyway, you've read my message,
so why aren't you replying?</i>

137
00:07:00,504 --> 00:07:02,339
[pleasant music playing]

138
00:07:23,068 --> 00:07:24,111
[beeps]

139
00:07:42,254 --> 00:07:44,590
Mr. Jung is having a meeting
with the car owner, right?

140
00:07:45,174 --> 00:07:48,342
Yes. Since the Safety Management
and Technical Investigation Teams

141
00:07:48,343 --> 00:07:51,470
are handling it, I was informed that
the final report will take a few days.

142
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:54,140
- [Yi-ji] Okay.
- Ms. Kang, the CEO wants to see you.

143
00:07:54,141 --> 00:07:55,392
Yes, I'll be right there.

144
00:07:58,061 --> 00:08:00,813
Ms. Im, you're acting like
Ms. Kang's personal secretary

145
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:02,899
instead of a employee of Legal Affairs.

146
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:05,359
I... I thought updating her
was part of my job.

147
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:08,779
Mm, I understand you're trying
to get on her good side,

148
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:12,492
but if you're going to do that,
why not ask to be her personal secretary?

149
00:08:13,911 --> 00:08:14,995
[scoffs]

150
00:08:15,662 --> 00:08:18,498
As you've probably heard,
Team 2 will handle this case.

151
00:08:19,458 --> 00:08:21,876
- Why is that?
- Why else? The case is urgent,

152
00:08:21,877 --> 00:08:23,586
so the company needs an expert like me.

153
00:08:23,587 --> 00:08:24,879
Have you seen the online post?

154
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:27,757
I mean, I spent the whole morning
scrambling to get it taken down,

155
00:08:27,758 --> 00:08:30,968
while you had time to leisurely visit
the car owner's wife in the hospital.

156
00:08:30,969 --> 00:08:32,262
[sighs dramatically]

157
00:08:32,804 --> 00:08:34,096
[boss] Mr. Jung.

158
00:08:34,097 --> 00:08:35,806
[sighs] Ah, yeah.

159
00:08:35,807 --> 00:08:36,849
[boss sighs]

160
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:38,809
It was the proper procedure
to show evidence

161
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:41,020
of us fulfilling the company's
moral responsibility.

162
00:08:41,021 --> 00:08:43,022
[Ki-tae] Procedure is fine.

163
00:08:43,023 --> 00:08:45,149
But in an unexpected case like this,

164
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:49,278
shouldn't quick thinking and flexible
handling of the situation come first?

165
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:50,988
I mean, just a little while ago,

166
00:08:50,989 --> 00:08:55,285
the car owner was so furious,
he flipped over the conference table,

167
00:08:55,911 --> 00:09:00,623
and it was I... I who managed
to steer him towards a settlement.

168
00:09:00,624 --> 00:09:01,582
[Ki-tae claps]

169
00:09:01,583 --> 00:09:03,876
A settlement before
we've even determined the cause?

170
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:05,127
That post needs to go.

171
00:09:05,128 --> 00:09:06,462
The Internet is going crazy.

172
00:09:06,463 --> 00:09:08,589
That's why I was asked to step in. Right?

173
00:09:08,590 --> 00:09:10,759
To what, pay damages
before an investigation?

174
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:12,301
[Ki-tae] So what?

175
00:09:12,302 --> 00:09:14,053
For now, that's the best option.

176
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:16,097
Mr. Song, this fire incident

177
00:09:16,098 --> 00:09:18,516
isn't something we can afford
to treat as a simple matter.

178
00:09:18,517 --> 00:09:21,352
Then, what? Do you want to make this
more complicated and escalate it?

179
00:09:21,353 --> 00:09:23,312
We should keep every possibility
open for now.

180
00:09:23,313 --> 00:09:25,439
We need to check for
any aftermarket modifications...

181
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,983
- [groans]
- ...or unauthorized wiring work,

182
00:09:26,984 --> 00:09:28,192
as well as any history of flooding.

183
00:09:28,193 --> 00:09:29,986
They said there weren't any!

184
00:09:29,987 --> 00:09:34,282
What if we drag this out for no reason and
end up with results that work against us?

185
00:09:34,283 --> 00:09:36,200
- What are you going to do then?
- Both of you, be quiet.

186
00:09:36,201 --> 00:09:39,537
We must determine the cause
before rushing into a settlement.

187
00:09:39,538 --> 00:09:41,664
Determining the cause
can be dealt with later.

188
00:09:41,665 --> 00:09:44,083
Right now, we need
to calm the customer down.

189
00:09:44,084 --> 00:09:47,420
It's because you keep insisting
on following principles

190
00:09:47,421 --> 00:09:49,130
that things don't work out in real life.

191
00:09:49,131 --> 00:09:51,049
With your approach,

192
00:09:51,717 --> 00:09:54,218
you'll never end up seeing this case
through to the end.

193
00:09:54,219 --> 00:09:55,137
I'll tell you that.

194
00:09:55,887 --> 00:09:57,055
Ms. Kang...

195
00:09:57,764 --> 00:09:58,932
[sighs deeply]

196
00:09:59,683 --> 00:10:02,852
The company is taking
a serious loss right now.

197
00:10:02,853 --> 00:10:06,939
Yes, in principle, we should settle
after identifying the case.

198
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:10,401
That way, the settlement amount
could change, right?

199
00:10:10,402 --> 00:10:12,779
Sir, the company's
profit and loss does matter,

200
00:10:13,822 --> 00:10:16,240
but an excessive settlement
meant to silence them

201
00:10:16,241 --> 00:10:19,118
while ignoring procedure
would set a bad precedent.

202
00:10:19,119 --> 00:10:22,289
It doesn't help resolve the problem
in the long term, either.

203
00:10:24,416 --> 00:10:25,916
[Byung-je] Hmm.

204
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:27,460
Get it resolved within the week.

205
00:10:27,461 --> 00:10:28,836
Procedure is important,

206
00:10:28,837 --> 00:10:34,592
but a case like this needs quick action,
as Mr. Jung Ki-tae says, right?

207
00:10:34,593 --> 00:10:36,511
Let's not cling
to something that won't work.

208
00:10:39,181 --> 00:10:42,809
If things are like this next week,
hand it over cleanly.

209
00:10:46,104 --> 00:10:49,399
Yes. In that case, I'll do my best, sir.

210
00:10:56,198 --> 00:10:57,323
There you are.

211
00:10:57,324 --> 00:10:59,116
How did the hospital visit go?

212
00:10:59,117 --> 00:11:02,370
What about breakfast?
If you skip it, it's bad.

213
00:11:02,371 --> 00:11:03,830
Didn't we agree to take a break?

214
00:11:06,124 --> 00:11:09,086
You look good together.
You make a good couple.

215
00:11:10,087 --> 00:11:13,964
Mr. Kim, when are you setting the date?

216
00:11:13,965 --> 00:11:15,758
Mr. Jung, honestly... [laughs]

217
00:11:15,759 --> 00:11:18,386
It seems things are pretty slow
at the Sales Team, huh?

218
00:11:18,387 --> 00:11:20,472
Seeing that you're lounging around here.

219
00:11:20,972 --> 00:11:22,723
I... I should get going now.

220
00:11:22,724 --> 00:11:24,101
- [Ki-tae] Yeah.
- See you.

221
00:11:27,562 --> 00:11:29,189
Ah, please don't be so cold.

222
00:11:29,773 --> 00:11:32,233
Mr. Kim may be a little short
on results, I know,

223
00:11:32,234 --> 00:11:33,901
but he's still a manager in Sales.

224
00:11:33,902 --> 00:11:35,194
That's not bad, is it?

225
00:11:35,195 --> 00:11:37,489
Be nice to him. Hmm?

226
00:11:45,497 --> 00:11:48,500
Do you think we're close enough
to talk about something like this?

227
00:11:49,751 --> 00:11:52,378
You realize
these are all sexist remarks, right?

228
00:11:52,379 --> 00:11:54,547
[laughs] Right.

229
00:11:54,548 --> 00:11:57,925
I understand that someone
who has been here forever, like you,

230
00:11:57,926 --> 00:12:00,428
- would resent a parachute hire like me.
- [laughs]

231
00:12:00,429 --> 00:12:01,971
Do you think that's the reason?

232
00:12:01,972 --> 00:12:04,974
Then what?
The manager position of Legal Affairs?

233
00:12:04,975 --> 00:12:06,684
Everyone says it's yours.

234
00:12:06,685 --> 00:12:08,478
They just haven't printed
your business cards yet.

235
00:12:09,813 --> 00:12:11,522
That manager position,

236
00:12:11,523 --> 00:12:13,775
it could be yours too, don't you think?

237
00:12:17,904 --> 00:12:19,613
Do you really think so?

238
00:12:19,614 --> 00:12:20,531
Of course,

239
00:12:20,532 --> 00:12:24,035
you'd have to have the basic skills
suited to that position, though.

240
00:12:24,995 --> 00:12:28,372
Also, please stop speaking
to me in that half-polite way

241
00:12:28,373 --> 00:12:30,082
just because we have the same rank.

242
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:32,502
We're both professionals here, aren't we?

243
00:12:37,507 --> 00:12:38,842
[upbeat music playing]

244
00:12:41,011 --> 00:12:42,429
[grunts in annoyance]

245
00:12:42,929 --> 00:12:44,848
- [sighs]
- [upbeat music fades]

246
00:12:47,642 --> 00:12:48,477
[clears throat]

247
00:12:57,068 --> 00:12:57,986
[exhales]

248
00:12:59,654 --> 00:13:00,655
Mom!

249
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:05,076
[door closes]

250
00:13:06,661 --> 00:13:08,663
[gentle music playing]

251
00:13:10,165 --> 00:13:12,209
HOW TO USE THE BLENDER

252
00:13:12,334 --> 00:13:14,835
HOW TO USE THE INDUCTION COOKTOP

253
00:13:14,836 --> 00:13:16,295
HOW TO USE THE MICROWAVE

254
00:13:16,296 --> 00:13:18,506
Every ingredient needs
a different temp and cooking time.

255
00:13:18,507 --> 00:13:20,049
You got to check them, Mom.

256
00:13:20,050 --> 00:13:22,427
Why did you buy so much fruit?

257
00:13:24,054 --> 00:13:26,514
But why did you buy split fruit?

258
00:13:26,515 --> 00:13:28,891
I don't know.
I just paid and grabbed them.

259
00:13:28,892 --> 00:13:30,393
Hmm? What? [laughs]

260
00:13:33,104 --> 00:13:34,647
Look, I added them.

261
00:13:34,648 --> 00:13:36,942
[laughs] Okay.

262
00:13:39,319 --> 00:13:42,071
- Hey, what's that smell?
- Hmm?

263
00:13:42,072 --> 00:13:45,491
[sniffs] Ah!
Oh, oh, that's right, that's right!

264
00:13:45,492 --> 00:13:47,994
Oh, no, no, no, no, no! Oh, ho!

265
00:13:48,537 --> 00:13:49,704
Oh!

266
00:13:50,747 --> 00:13:55,292
Oh! And I made samgyetang
because you were coming over,

267
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:57,586
but you didn't even get to eat any.

268
00:13:57,587 --> 00:14:00,005
[sighs] I told you I'd do the cooking.

269
00:14:00,006 --> 00:14:02,466
- Oh.
- You just go and sit down.

270
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:04,386
Oh, goodness!

271
00:14:07,222 --> 00:14:09,974
Oh, right.
Your birthday is coming up, Mom.

272
00:14:09,975 --> 00:14:12,268
- What should I get you?
- Mm...

273
00:14:12,269 --> 00:14:15,229
I don't want to say this
because you have a soft spot for me.

274
00:14:15,230 --> 00:14:16,982
What is it? Just tell me, Mom.

275
00:14:19,609 --> 00:14:20,859
When your dad was alive,

276
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,570
I used to hand him the shoehorn

277
00:14:22,571 --> 00:14:25,531
and straighten his tie
whenever he left for work.

278
00:14:25,532 --> 00:14:27,950
Back then, I took that for granted.

279
00:14:27,951 --> 00:14:31,745
These days, when I see people
pouring out at lunchtime... [sighs]

280
00:14:31,746 --> 00:14:36,667
Oh, I can't help wishing my son
was right here, like your dad used to be.

281
00:14:36,668 --> 00:14:37,836
You've graduated now.

282
00:14:38,545 --> 00:14:40,546
And there's a time for everything.

283
00:14:40,547 --> 00:14:41,798
You can operate your...

284
00:14:42,924 --> 00:14:45,134
Yes, your online jewelry business later,

285
00:14:45,135 --> 00:14:46,385
but getting a job--

286
00:14:46,386 --> 00:14:48,053
Mom, you mentioned that before.

287
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:51,265
I sent my résumé out.
Maybe something will happen.

288
00:14:51,266 --> 00:14:53,100
[excitedly] Oh!

289
00:14:53,101 --> 00:14:54,561
You'll get hired for sure!

290
00:14:55,186 --> 00:14:56,770
If I were the interviewer,

291
00:14:56,771 --> 00:14:59,148
I'd give my son a perfect score
and hire him.

292
00:14:59,149 --> 00:15:00,691
[laughs] Good job, good job.

293
00:15:00,692 --> 00:15:01,900
[both laugh]

294
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:03,152
Don't celebrate yet.

295
00:15:03,153 --> 00:15:05,070
[laughs] I'll cut you some fruit.

296
00:15:05,071 --> 00:15:06,740
[laughs excitedly, sighs]

297
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:14,121
[female manager] <i>How about switching
to a more provocative genre?</i>

298
00:15:14,122 --> 00:15:16,624
<i>These days,
people want something more immediate.</i>

299
00:15:16,625 --> 00:15:19,335
<i>Either make it bold
or change direction completely.</i>

300
00:15:19,336 --> 00:15:21,379
<i>Who looks at this
kind of stuff these days?</i>

301
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:24,298
- [cell phone vibrating]
- [groans]

302
00:15:24,299 --> 00:15:25,216
MOM

303
00:15:26,176 --> 00:15:27,843
- Yeah, Mom.
<i>- I sent you the money.</i>

304
00:15:27,844 --> 00:15:30,430
Oh, really? Thank you.

305
00:15:31,014 --> 00:15:33,391
I'll make it big soon
and take good care of you.

306
00:15:34,017 --> 00:15:36,143
<i>I barely managed to persuade your father.</i>

307
00:15:36,144 --> 00:15:37,519
You've got a year.

308
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:39,438
If you can't get a job by then,

309
00:15:39,439 --> 00:15:41,607
come back home
and help your dad with his work.

310
00:15:41,608 --> 00:15:43,108
[man] <i>Ah, yes. I know.</i>

311
00:15:43,109 --> 00:15:44,652
Please stop worrying.

312
00:15:44,653 --> 00:15:46,487
How can I not worry?

313
00:15:46,488 --> 00:15:49,407
Everyone I meet asks
what my son is doing in Seoul.

314
00:15:50,283 --> 00:15:51,283
<i>Ah, just hang up.</i>

315
00:15:51,284 --> 00:15:53,285
<i>- There's no point talking to you.</i>
- Huh?

316
00:15:53,286 --> 00:15:54,913
Hey, Mom...

317
00:15:58,667 --> 00:16:00,418
[cell phone vibrating]

318
00:16:01,044 --> 00:16:02,212
SUN-WOO

319
00:16:03,254 --> 00:16:05,798
[sighs] Did you get rejected again?

320
00:16:05,799 --> 00:16:08,968
Chicken and beer won't cut it.
We need something better for us tonight.

321
00:16:10,261 --> 00:16:12,180
Go and put on your best outfit.

322
00:16:18,144 --> 00:16:19,895
LEGAL AFFAIRS SENIOR MANAGER
KANG YI-JI

323
00:16:19,896 --> 00:16:21,189
MANAGER KIM DONG-SEOK

324
00:16:21,773 --> 00:16:24,734
- [cell phone vibrating]
- [mouse clicking]

325
00:16:29,698 --> 00:16:31,490
BASE MODEL
NO OPTIONAL FEATURES SELECTED

326
00:16:31,491 --> 00:16:35,494
If this is a vehicle without any options,
it doesn't have a remote start function.

327
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:36,913
TEAM LEADER KIM MIN-SEOP

328
00:16:37,622 --> 00:16:38,748
[cell phone vibrating]

329
00:16:39,374 --> 00:16:41,375
Yes, Mr. Kim. How did it go?

330
00:16:41,376 --> 00:16:42,710
[Min-seop] <i>Yes, Ms. Kang.</i>

331
00:16:42,711 --> 00:16:44,420
<i>It's in a worse state than expected,</i>

332
00:16:44,421 --> 00:16:47,131
<i>so a detailed inspection will likely
take at least another week.</i>

333
00:16:47,132 --> 00:16:49,216
But I'm looking at the CCTV footage now,

334
00:16:49,217 --> 00:16:52,387
and the car's smart key
doesn't match the factory specifications.

335
00:16:52,971 --> 00:16:54,388
Can we find out its modification history?

336
00:16:54,389 --> 00:16:57,141
<i>If they only used private repair shops,
there won't be any digital records.</i>

337
00:16:57,142 --> 00:16:59,685
<i>The only option is to track down
the shop that did the work.</i>

338
00:16:59,686 --> 00:17:00,936
Huh.

339
00:17:00,937 --> 00:17:02,480
I understand.

340
00:17:03,106 --> 00:17:04,107
[line disconnects]

341
00:17:05,442 --> 00:17:07,110
24 MISSED CALLS
MANAGER KIM DONG-SEOK

342
00:17:18,955 --> 00:17:20,331
[woman] So cute.

343
00:17:20,874 --> 00:17:22,667
Goodness, we were so young.

344
00:17:23,793 --> 00:17:24,710
[chuckles softly]

345
00:17:24,711 --> 00:17:25,754
HUSBAND
TEXT MESSAGE

346
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:30,799
I'M SORRY. I'VE BEEN SO OUT OF IT.
I COMPLETELY FORGOT.

347
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:33,552
[husband] <i>Happy birthday.
I'm sorry I can't be there with you.</i>

348
00:17:33,553 --> 00:17:35,555
<i>Go shopping and have fun.</i>

349
00:17:43,396 --> 00:17:45,355
- Happy birthday!
- Aw!

350
00:17:45,356 --> 00:17:49,234
Gosh. You're always so busy,
but you came on time today.

351
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:52,112
Yi-ji, I'm still in my 20s at heart.

352
00:17:52,113 --> 00:17:54,657
Let's just use two big candles,
for appearances.

353
00:17:55,658 --> 00:17:57,910
Oh, no. I bought
the right number of candles.

354
00:17:57,911 --> 00:18:02,081
Mm. It's all right. I can
switch 'em around, just like this.

355
00:18:02,624 --> 00:18:04,542
[laughs]

356
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:06,585
Which one is it today?

357
00:18:06,586 --> 00:18:09,297
Today... is number two.

358
00:18:09,798 --> 00:18:10,839
Working late again?

359
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:13,175
The day before yesterday,
it was numbers one and three.

360
00:18:13,176 --> 00:18:15,553
He met with a vendor
and went on a business trip.

361
00:18:16,888 --> 00:18:19,223
- Ah.
- Well, how are things with you?

362
00:18:19,224 --> 00:18:21,099
Things still the same?

363
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:24,228
I asked for some time apart,
but he keeps contacting me.

364
00:18:24,229 --> 00:18:27,856
[sighs] It's not that you two
don't suit each other.

365
00:18:27,857 --> 00:18:31,276
But... [sighs] I don't know. I'm sorry.

366
00:18:31,277 --> 00:18:33,195
[both laugh]

367
00:18:33,196 --> 00:18:36,573
I don't know. He's like a pair of shoes
that hurts every time I wear them.

368
00:18:36,574 --> 00:18:38,325
Uncomfortable.

369
00:18:38,326 --> 00:18:41,411
New shoes need to be broken in
a bit before they fit.

370
00:18:41,412 --> 00:18:43,622
Who comes tailor-made
right from the start?

371
00:18:43,623 --> 00:18:46,750
If you nitpick everything the way you do,
you'll never date anybody.

372
00:18:46,751 --> 00:18:47,751
Marriage is the same.

373
00:18:47,752 --> 00:18:50,003
You've got to take the plunge
while you're still immature

374
00:18:50,004 --> 00:18:51,630
- and as clueless as I am.
- I don't know.

375
00:18:51,631 --> 00:18:53,173
I'm hungry. Let's eat.

376
00:18:53,174 --> 00:18:55,759
Okay, let's really treat ourselves today.

377
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:57,803
For my husband
who's on someone else's side

378
00:18:57,804 --> 00:19:00,473
and handing over his credit card
for his wife's birthday.

379
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:02,599
What do you want to eat?

380
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:05,019
Since the card belongs to him,
let's get the most expensive meal.

381
00:19:05,603 --> 00:19:07,397
Excuse me. We'd like to order.

382
00:19:09,941 --> 00:19:11,401
Two special courses, please.

383
00:19:12,402 --> 00:19:13,653
[scoffs] Is that your best outfit?

384
00:19:14,571 --> 00:19:15,946
What? It's new.

385
00:19:15,947 --> 00:19:17,364
I took the tag off today.

386
00:19:17,365 --> 00:19:18,991
It's not your best, but your favorite.

387
00:19:18,992 --> 00:19:21,451
Welcome. How many are in your party?

388
00:19:21,452 --> 00:19:24,413
- Just us two.
- Ah, right this way, please.

389
00:19:24,414 --> 00:19:25,831
Okay.

390
00:19:25,832 --> 00:19:27,416
All right, I'll help you with your order.

391
00:19:27,417 --> 00:19:29,042
[laughs] Thank you.

392
00:19:29,043 --> 00:19:30,628
[sighs]

393
00:19:32,255 --> 00:19:33,840
[Sun-woo gasps]

394
00:19:35,967 --> 00:19:38,176
- Let's leave.
- Let's order the cheapest thing.

395
00:19:38,177 --> 00:19:39,219
- No, no, no.
- Yes?

396
00:19:39,220 --> 00:19:43,348
I mean... [laughs]
I drank way too much whisky yesterday.

397
00:19:43,349 --> 00:19:45,351
Ah, then... wine?

398
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:48,729
- I also had too much wine yesterday.
- [snaps fingers] Then beer.

399
00:19:48,730 --> 00:19:49,981
[snaps fingers]

400
00:19:52,734 --> 00:19:54,151
Yes. Two bottles, please.

401
00:19:54,152 --> 00:19:56,738
- [waitress] Here are your beers.
- [Tae-jun] Thank you.

402
00:19:59,490 --> 00:20:01,366
Wow, this place is no joke.

403
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:04,036
One night here would wipe out
a month of my expenses.

404
00:20:04,037 --> 00:20:06,747
What, we can't come to a place like this?

405
00:20:06,748 --> 00:20:09,750
I heard your business partner
ran off with the money.

406
00:20:09,751 --> 00:20:12,044
Today was the worst
for other reasons, too.

407
00:20:12,045 --> 00:20:13,337
Let's live it up a bit.

408
00:20:13,338 --> 00:20:15,589
Whoa, hey! Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Wait, wait, wait!

409
00:20:15,590 --> 00:20:16,841
What?

410
00:20:20,929 --> 00:20:23,097
- [laughs]
- Give it here.

411
00:20:25,183 --> 00:20:28,268
[sighs] Tae-jun, I know
you're having a hard time, okay?

412
00:20:28,269 --> 00:20:29,811
I can get through it, really.

413
00:20:29,812 --> 00:20:32,397
Here, buddy.
Just get it off your chest, all right?

414
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:33,690
[Tae-jun] Cheers!

415
00:20:33,691 --> 00:20:34,901
[Tae-jun laughs]

416
00:20:37,946 --> 00:20:39,696
[both sigh]

417
00:20:39,697 --> 00:20:41,574
You're so thoroughly prepared.

418
00:20:42,116 --> 00:20:43,992
Isn't that why you came prepared too?

419
00:20:43,993 --> 00:20:45,327
What do you mean?

420
00:20:45,328 --> 00:20:46,788
Why did you buy so much fruit?

421
00:20:47,664 --> 00:20:49,456
Fruit is expensive.

422
00:20:49,457 --> 00:20:50,959
Here.

423
00:20:54,504 --> 00:20:55,629
- Mm!
- [waitress] Excuse me, sir.

424
00:20:55,630 --> 00:20:58,633
Outside food isn't allowed.
Would you like to order a fruit platter?

425
00:20:59,342 --> 00:21:00,635
No. I didn't eat it.

426
00:21:04,639 --> 00:21:06,015
I didn't eat any of it yet.

427
00:21:06,766 --> 00:21:08,726
- [laughs awkwardly]
- Put it back in.

428
00:21:09,936 --> 00:21:11,479
What is this doing here?

429
00:21:13,564 --> 00:21:15,065
Hey, how can you eat that for real?

430
00:21:15,066 --> 00:21:17,110
[laughs] Wow, that was a close call.

431
00:21:18,569 --> 00:21:21,572
[tsks] I heard she even took your deposit.

432
00:21:22,156 --> 00:21:23,824
Your online store was
finally getting established.

433
00:21:23,825 --> 00:21:24,783
What was the problem?

434
00:21:24,784 --> 00:21:27,536
She's going to go study abroad
with her boyfriend.

435
00:21:27,537 --> 00:21:29,122
- I can't stop her.
- [sighs]

436
00:21:30,248 --> 00:21:31,999
And... the money?

437
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,961
I poured my blood, sweat,
and tears into that business.

438
00:21:35,628 --> 00:21:37,587
Do you know what it's like
to get backstabbed by your partner?

439
00:21:37,588 --> 00:21:38,965
Uh, I wouldn't know.

440
00:21:39,632 --> 00:21:40,882
What about the money?

441
00:21:40,883 --> 00:21:44,052
[sighs] Do I need to get a job
so I can start over?

442
00:21:44,053 --> 00:21:45,012
Getting a job is good.

443
00:21:45,013 --> 00:21:46,972
- So what about the money?
- Right, money!

444
00:21:46,973 --> 00:21:48,432
I'm getting a job because of money.

445
00:21:48,433 --> 00:21:50,393
- Cheers!
- [sighs]

446
00:21:51,853 --> 00:21:53,228
Gosh!

447
00:21:53,229 --> 00:21:55,314
You worked so hard to save up that cash.

448
00:21:59,610 --> 00:22:00,652
[sighs heavily]

449
00:22:00,653 --> 00:22:05,949
- Hey, where there are a lot of people...
- [grunts]

450
00:22:05,950 --> 00:22:07,702
...usually, you know...

451
00:22:11,289 --> 00:22:12,290
[glasses clink]

452
00:22:13,541 --> 00:22:15,585
[band playing upbeat music]

453
00:22:16,627 --> 00:22:18,171
Something's going on.

454
00:22:33,853 --> 00:22:35,772
- [upbeat music stops]
- Whoo!

455
00:22:40,276 --> 00:22:42,944
[band playing romantic music]

456
00:22:42,945 --> 00:22:44,447
[Yi-ji] Don't. Stop, please.

457
00:22:56,250 --> 00:22:59,337
Yi-ji, today is
the 100th day of us dating.

458
00:23:01,297 --> 00:23:02,799
Will you marry me?

459
00:23:04,425 --> 00:23:05,425
[onlooker cheers]

460
00:23:05,426 --> 00:23:07,552
[crowd] Say yes! Say yes! Say yes!

461
00:23:07,553 --> 00:23:09,054
Are you crazy?

462
00:23:09,055 --> 00:23:10,514
Today is Ji-won's birthday.

463
00:23:10,515 --> 00:23:14,392
Don't... don't mind me.
It's so romantic. [laughs]

464
00:23:14,393 --> 00:23:15,520
Really.

465
00:23:16,729 --> 00:23:20,483
I'll stay by your side
for the rest of my life, okay?

466
00:23:21,150 --> 00:23:22,151
You have to answer.

467
00:23:22,819 --> 00:23:24,821
[Sun-woo] This marriage
ain't ever gonna work!

468
00:23:27,865 --> 00:23:30,201
- [music fades]
- Ah, wait.

469
00:23:33,037 --> 00:23:34,830
You should reconsider.

470
00:23:34,831 --> 00:23:36,414
[Sun-woo laughs]

471
00:23:36,415 --> 00:23:39,334
[Yi-ji] I'll give this back
when you buy me a new one.

472
00:23:39,335 --> 00:23:42,337
You'll regret it for the rest of your life
if you marry her!

473
00:23:42,338 --> 00:23:46,133
- She's so cold-hearted. [laughs]
- Who is he?

474
00:23:46,134 --> 00:23:48,094
- Who the hell are you?
- Dong-seok, stop it.

475
00:23:49,929 --> 00:23:52,681
- [band playing lively music]
- [Sun-woo] Hmm?

476
00:23:52,682 --> 00:23:55,184
[Sun-woo laughing]

477
00:24:00,189 --> 00:24:01,898
Yi-ji, Yi-ji. You know I love you, right?

478
00:24:01,899 --> 00:24:04,317
- You're the only one for me.
- Whoa! No! No

479
00:24:04,318 --> 00:24:07,863
Grabbing somebody's hand
by force like that is assault.

480
00:24:07,864 --> 00:24:14,703
[exclaims] It's two years in prison,
or a fine of up to five million won.

481
00:24:14,704 --> 00:24:15,787
Right?

482
00:24:15,788 --> 00:24:18,165
- [cackles]
- I asked you who the hell you are!

483
00:24:18,166 --> 00:24:21,668
I'm... I'm sorry. He's my friend.
He's had too much to drink. I'm sorry.

484
00:24:21,669 --> 00:24:23,712
Hey, hey, wait, wait, wait.
Let go, let go.

485
00:24:23,713 --> 00:24:27,592
Come on, this person here would
really hate you grabbing her like that.

486
00:24:28,176 --> 00:24:33,347
She said there's no point in holding on
to someone whose heart has moved on.

487
00:24:34,140 --> 00:24:36,474
She thinks that... [sobbing]

488
00:24:36,475 --> 00:24:38,351
[Tae-jun] Hey, what...
what's wrong with you?

489
00:24:38,352 --> 00:24:40,520
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. Uh, I'm sorry.

490
00:24:40,521 --> 00:24:41,646
I'm sorry. Let's go.

491
00:24:41,647 --> 00:24:43,398
- [Sun-woo laughing]
- I'm sorry.

492
00:24:43,399 --> 00:24:46,109
Yi-ji, what should I do?
Report him to the police? Should I?

493
00:24:46,110 --> 00:24:47,444
Okay. I'll do that. I will.

494
00:24:47,445 --> 00:24:49,071
[band stops playing]

495
00:24:51,449 --> 00:24:52,782
Thank you very much.

496
00:24:52,783 --> 00:24:55,703
- We'll have a good life. Thank you.
- [scattered applause]

497
00:25:06,297 --> 00:25:08,758
What do you think? It's my gift.

498
00:25:09,383 --> 00:25:10,550
This place faces south.

499
00:25:10,551 --> 00:25:12,219
THANK YOU FOR ACCEPTING
MY MARRIAGE PROPOSAL

500
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:14,221
There's a supermarket,
a kindergarten, and a school nearby.

501
00:25:14,222 --> 00:25:16,598
It's the perfect place for newlyweds.

502
00:25:16,599 --> 00:25:17,682
I paid the deposit.

503
00:25:17,683 --> 00:25:19,851
With our salaries,
we'll pay it off quickly.

504
00:25:19,852 --> 00:25:23,104
We've been dating for three months
and you ask me to marry you?

505
00:25:23,105 --> 00:25:24,357
Uh...

506
00:25:25,066 --> 00:25:27,443
A hundred days isn't a short time.

507
00:25:28,444 --> 00:25:31,072
Tell me, why on earth
do you want to marry me?

508
00:25:32,865 --> 00:25:34,491
Well, you're pretty good at your job.

509
00:25:34,492 --> 00:25:36,953
You have similar abilities and rank to me.

510
00:25:39,038 --> 00:25:41,456
You want to get married
for such dumb reasons?

511
00:25:41,457 --> 00:25:43,833
I can accommodate you with everything.

512
00:25:43,834 --> 00:25:45,502
That's how everyone dates.

513
00:25:45,503 --> 00:25:48,547
Then you get married, have kids,
raise them and all that.

514
00:25:50,007 --> 00:25:51,175
[gasps] Please, just...

515
00:25:52,468 --> 00:25:54,135
Let's end this.

516
00:25:54,136 --> 00:25:55,554
I came here to say that.

517
00:25:56,180 --> 00:25:58,056
You ignored me when I asked for a break,

518
00:25:58,057 --> 00:26:00,433
then showed up out of the blue
and pushed me to get married.

519
00:26:00,434 --> 00:26:02,561
Is that your idea of accommodating me?

520
00:26:03,688 --> 00:26:06,481
Uh... I'll do better. I can do better.

521
00:26:06,482 --> 00:26:07,983
- You'll see.
- [sighs in exasperation]

522
00:26:07,984 --> 00:26:09,985
You follow me around at work
so I can't get anything done,

523
00:26:09,986 --> 00:26:12,112
egging on the people around me,
trying to please them.

524
00:26:12,113 --> 00:26:13,863
That's your idea of doing better?

525
00:26:13,864 --> 00:26:16,241
[sighs] That's how I show my love.

526
00:26:16,242 --> 00:26:19,494
No, you're just looking for a woman
who meets your criteria,

527
00:26:19,495 --> 00:26:22,414
someone to buy a house with
and help pay off the mortgage.

528
00:26:22,415 --> 00:26:24,332
Of course, I'm not saying that's wrong.

529
00:26:24,333 --> 00:26:26,751
In fact, I used to think
the same way, too.

530
00:26:26,752 --> 00:26:28,421
But I don't anymore.

531
00:26:29,088 --> 00:26:31,507
Let's just stop wasting time and break up.

532
00:26:32,675 --> 00:26:34,010
[Yi-ji grunts]

533
00:26:37,972 --> 00:26:41,182
Kang Yi-ji, do you think I'm going
to cling to you if you act like this?

534
00:26:41,183 --> 00:26:43,602
Do you think
that you're much better than me?

535
00:26:44,353 --> 00:26:47,480
Yi-ji, you need to know your place.

536
00:26:47,481 --> 00:26:49,899
There are women who are prettier than you,
more than you can count.

537
00:26:49,900 --> 00:26:53,528
You're old enough to get turned away
by a matchmaking agency.

538
00:26:53,529 --> 00:26:54,696
Stop acting so superior.

539
00:26:54,697 --> 00:26:56,741
- You're only a senior manager, after all--
- What?

540
00:26:57,616 --> 00:26:58,826
[sighs]

541
00:27:00,369 --> 00:27:03,663
You won't make general manager.

542
00:27:03,664 --> 00:27:06,207
Mr. Song already picked Mr. Jung over you.

543
00:27:06,208 --> 00:27:09,794
At work, the one who knows how
to please the boss comes out on top.

544
00:27:09,795 --> 00:27:11,881
That's what you're the worst at. Come on.

545
00:27:12,590 --> 00:27:13,841
You gotta face reality.

546
00:27:14,675 --> 00:27:16,594
For you, someone like me
is the best choice.

547
00:27:17,345 --> 00:27:18,554
Don't you get it yet?

548
00:27:19,263 --> 00:27:20,931
[melancholy music playing]

549
00:27:24,226 --> 00:27:26,603
[sighs] Thanks to what you said,

550
00:27:26,604 --> 00:27:29,190
now I know what my reality looks like.

551
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:45,206
[melancholy music continues]

552
00:27:54,423 --> 00:27:55,633
[scoffs]

553
00:27:57,218 --> 00:27:59,345
[upbeat music playing]

554
00:28:16,946 --> 00:28:19,281
[cell phone vibrating]

555
00:28:29,583 --> 00:28:30,876
[sighs softly]

556
00:28:31,669 --> 00:28:32,919
[sighs]

557
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:34,380
[groggily] Hello?

558
00:28:35,756 --> 00:28:36,756
A job interview?

559
00:28:36,757 --> 00:28:40,510
[gasps] Oh, of course.
I'll be right there!

560
00:28:40,511 --> 00:28:42,887
CHRONIC MOTORS INTERNSHIP INTERVIEW
APRIL 2, 10 A.M.

561
00:28:42,888 --> 00:28:44,722
Damn it. Hey, I missed
the text they sent earlier.

562
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:46,683
- I gotta go.
- [Tae-jun] Good luck.

563
00:28:46,684 --> 00:28:49,102
I've sent in over 50 applications
and haven't had a single text yet.

564
00:28:49,103 --> 00:28:52,273
Clothes! Clothes! Clothes!
Clothes! Clothes! Clothes! Clothes!

565
00:28:53,399 --> 00:28:54,858
Hey, that's mine!

566
00:28:54,859 --> 00:28:57,610
- Oh, let me borrow it once.
- Hey! Hey!

567
00:28:57,611 --> 00:28:59,613
Oh, is this toothbrush yours or mine?

568
00:29:04,368 --> 00:29:06,412
[upbeat music continues]

569
00:29:08,664 --> 00:29:10,666
INTERVIEW ROOM

570
00:29:15,671 --> 00:29:16,964
POSITION APPLIED FOR
LEGAL AFFAIRS INTERN

571
00:29:18,716 --> 00:29:20,134
- [woman] Mr. Lee Ji-woong.
- Yes.

572
00:29:26,432 --> 00:29:28,267
- [Sun-woo grunts]
- [door opens]

573
00:29:30,769 --> 00:29:32,313
- Ms. Choi Yu-jin.
- Yes.

574
00:29:33,647 --> 00:29:34,857
INTERVIEW ROOM

575
00:29:35,691 --> 00:29:36,692
[sighs]

576
00:29:38,360 --> 00:29:40,154
APPLICATION FORM
HAN SUN-WOO

577
00:29:44,325 --> 00:29:45,783
[clears throat]

578
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:46,994
[door opens]

579
00:29:48,537 --> 00:29:49,955
[sighs]

580
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:54,918
Oh, uh... excuse me.
There's still one more interview.

581
00:29:54,919 --> 00:29:56,961
Oh, I'm sorry. Our interviews are over.

582
00:29:56,962 --> 00:29:58,755
What?

583
00:29:58,756 --> 00:30:00,883
- Please check again.
- I'm sorry.

584
00:30:01,592 --> 00:30:03,009
[upbeat music playing]

585
00:30:03,010 --> 00:30:05,178
That can't be right. Just a moment.

586
00:30:05,179 --> 00:30:07,096
[gasps] Hey, you can't go in there!

587
00:30:07,097 --> 00:30:08,015
Excuse me.

588
00:30:09,433 --> 00:30:11,100
[woman] You can't do this here.

589
00:30:11,101 --> 00:30:13,770
Also, following and threatening
someone like this is a crime.

590
00:30:13,771 --> 00:30:14,771
It's considered stalking.

591
00:30:14,772 --> 00:30:18,317
You'll regret it for the rest of your life
if you marry her!

592
00:30:21,612 --> 00:30:22,695
What is it?

593
00:30:22,696 --> 00:30:23,988
You haven't seen me yet.

594
00:30:23,989 --> 00:30:26,909
I felt I'd seen enough,
so I rejected your application.

595
00:30:28,494 --> 00:30:31,163
You get to decide the outcome,
but I should get a chance.

596
00:30:33,207 --> 00:30:35,125
All right. Sit down.

597
00:30:45,761 --> 00:30:47,846
Do you know what the job entails?

598
00:30:48,430 --> 00:30:49,932
Yeah, it's assisting
the Legal Affairs Team.

599
00:30:52,601 --> 00:30:55,062
What do you think?
Do you expect me to hire you?

600
00:30:55,646 --> 00:30:58,357
I believe you'll give me
a fair assessment.

601
00:31:01,986 --> 00:31:04,280
There's a lot of emotion involved
in your case analysis.

602
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:07,907
You also said you prioritize the parties'
emotional stability in mediation.

603
00:31:07,908 --> 00:31:09,951
It was an important matter.

604
00:31:09,952 --> 00:31:13,246
I judged that realistic
problem-solving was only possible

605
00:31:13,247 --> 00:31:14,455
when they were emotionally stable.

606
00:31:14,456 --> 00:31:18,210
In Legal Affairs, minimizing risk
takes priority over emotions.

607
00:31:18,794 --> 00:31:22,046
I think emotions can't be excluded
from anything people do.

608
00:31:22,047 --> 00:31:25,216
Calming their emotions first to reduce
the cost and time of the dispute

609
00:31:25,217 --> 00:31:26,968
was, to me, a more rational choice.

610
00:31:26,969 --> 00:31:30,722
Who takes responsibility if you can't
keep those emotions under control?

611
00:31:30,723 --> 00:31:32,849
That's why I gathered data too.

612
00:31:32,850 --> 00:31:35,893
To prove that my judgment wasn't
based on personal feelings,

613
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:39,773
but was objectively beneficial in terms
of the time and costs involved.

614
00:31:46,697 --> 00:31:48,823
You've only just
graduated from university,

615
00:31:48,824 --> 00:31:50,450
have no internship experience,

616
00:31:50,451 --> 00:31:52,410
show tendencies toward dating violence,

617
00:31:52,411 --> 00:31:54,245
and can't even control your drinking.

618
00:31:54,246 --> 00:31:56,122
Do you think you're qualified
to be my assistant?

619
00:31:56,123 --> 00:31:58,708
Yesterday, I was just
unwinding with a friend.

620
00:31:58,709 --> 00:32:01,878
- I don't usually drink that much...
- [chuckles] That's all right.

621
00:32:01,879 --> 00:32:06,090
You're not here to explain yourself
or make excuses.

622
00:32:06,091 --> 00:32:10,345
But I... approach legal affairs
based on solid evidence and standards,

623
00:32:10,346 --> 00:32:12,847
not emotions.

624
00:32:12,848 --> 00:32:15,016
I believe that's something
you could teach me over time.

625
00:32:15,017 --> 00:32:16,100
Teach you what?

626
00:32:16,101 --> 00:32:19,270
If a company pays to hire an employee,
it should put them to work.

627
00:32:19,271 --> 00:32:21,230
A company isn't a training school.

628
00:32:21,231 --> 00:32:23,066
It's okay to be a little inexperienced.

629
00:32:23,067 --> 00:32:24,984
Some people are good from the start.

630
00:32:24,985 --> 00:32:27,529
We hold interviews like this
to hire those people.

631
00:32:28,989 --> 00:32:32,368
Unfortunately, Mr. Han Sun-woo,
you don't meet our hiring criteria.

632
00:32:33,702 --> 00:32:36,412
If this is about yesterday,
accept my apology.

633
00:32:36,413 --> 00:32:37,914
I'll accept your apology.

634
00:32:37,915 --> 00:32:40,918
But my decision is not going to change.

635
00:32:41,502 --> 00:32:44,087
[sighs] Hey, you were
a new employee once too.

636
00:32:44,088 --> 00:32:45,422
I can do a good job.

637
00:32:46,048 --> 00:32:48,966
If you came here to do something
you've never done before,

638
00:32:48,967 --> 00:32:51,678
then you should've made an effort
like you've never made before.

639
00:32:51,679 --> 00:32:53,097
At least that's what I did.

640
00:32:57,851 --> 00:32:59,103
[door opens]

641
00:32:59,895 --> 00:33:01,187
- [sighs]
- [door closes]

642
00:33:01,188 --> 00:33:03,482
[mellow music playing]

643
00:33:14,076 --> 00:33:16,577
[Eun-ha, softly]
Everything looks good there.

644
00:33:16,578 --> 00:33:18,914
And next is a hibiscus tea.

645
00:33:23,502 --> 00:33:25,462
Huh? You're Han Sun-woo, right?

646
00:33:26,046 --> 00:33:28,047
- Im Eun-ha! It's been a while.
- [laughs]

647
00:33:28,048 --> 00:33:29,924
What's this?
Did you come for an interview?

648
00:33:29,925 --> 00:33:31,801
[sighs] I didn't get it.

649
00:33:31,802 --> 00:33:34,637
- Do you work here?
- Mm. It's my second year.

650
00:33:34,638 --> 00:33:37,140
Wow, what a surprise,
running into the Milky Way.

651
00:33:37,141 --> 00:33:39,559
What? I thought my nickname was Sewer.

652
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:40,685
It was Milky Way?

653
00:33:40,686 --> 00:33:42,646
To Tae-jun, you were the Milky Way.

654
00:33:44,523 --> 00:33:46,190
Are... you in touch with Tae-jun?

655
00:33:46,191 --> 00:33:47,526
We live together.

656
00:33:48,485 --> 00:33:49,486
[Eun-ha] Mm.

657
00:33:50,779 --> 00:33:53,698
I'm on a coffee errand.
Want to get a cup with me?

658
00:33:53,699 --> 00:33:55,199
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

659
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:57,702
Don't take it to heart.
Get back out there.

660
00:33:57,703 --> 00:34:00,997
Even if you get hired,
you still have to wait to be a full-timer.

661
00:34:00,998 --> 00:34:05,042
[sighs] You were the wise one,
starting work early and all.

662
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:06,837
Me? I didn't give it much thought.

663
00:34:07,546 --> 00:34:11,257
I was passing by and saw
these people coming out at lunchtime,

664
00:34:11,258 --> 00:34:14,469
[sighs] with their IDs around their necks.

665
00:34:14,470 --> 00:34:17,930
I thought,
"That's what adult life looks like."

666
00:34:17,931 --> 00:34:20,391
- That dream was what gave me a goal.
- [laughs]

667
00:34:20,392 --> 00:34:21,769
I get the dream.

668
00:34:23,562 --> 00:34:28,065
But that senior manager
seemed pretty intimidating.

669
00:34:28,066 --> 00:34:29,692
Hey, she certainly is not.

670
00:34:29,693 --> 00:34:31,360
Ms. Kang is a 100% "T".

671
00:34:31,361 --> 00:34:32,695
A total capital "T".

672
00:34:32,696 --> 00:34:34,697
Well, almost 100%.

673
00:34:34,698 --> 00:34:37,493
But she's a warm person
once you get to know her.

674
00:34:39,328 --> 00:34:40,453
Warm, you say?

675
00:34:40,454 --> 00:34:42,247
[exclaims]

676
00:34:43,957 --> 00:34:46,667
I learned all the practical work from her
over the past two years.

677
00:34:46,668 --> 00:34:49,253
She taught me really well,
even though she was busy.

678
00:34:49,254 --> 00:34:51,714
She's a little on edge
because something serious happened

679
00:34:51,715 --> 00:34:53,634
just when she's up for a promotion.

680
00:34:54,426 --> 00:34:55,635
- Serious?
- [buzzing]

681
00:34:55,636 --> 00:34:57,387
Oh, forget it. [chuckles]

682
00:35:03,560 --> 00:35:05,020
What is it?

683
00:35:10,776 --> 00:35:12,652
This is the space for Unit 702,

684
00:35:12,653 --> 00:35:15,364
but we didn't have any flood damage
during that rain.

685
00:35:16,448 --> 00:35:17,865
You received our letter, right?

686
00:35:17,866 --> 00:35:18,950
I know it's a bother,

687
00:35:18,951 --> 00:35:21,661
but I'd like all the CCTV footage
for the month if you could, please.

688
00:35:21,662 --> 00:35:24,956
Oh, I have to speak to my supervisor
about that, but it's lunchtime now.

689
00:35:24,957 --> 00:35:26,582
Would you like to wait
in the control room?

690
00:35:26,583 --> 00:35:27,584
Yes, I can do that.

691
00:35:34,967 --> 00:35:36,677
PLIÉ FOREST BALLET ACADEMY

692
00:35:37,678 --> 00:35:40,597
[Yi-ji] <i>They just have two sons,
but a ballet academy?</i>

693
00:35:54,278 --> 00:35:55,445
[door opens]

694
00:35:57,656 --> 00:36:00,200
- Hey, you asked for me?
- Oh, hello. How are you?

695
00:36:03,370 --> 00:36:04,663
[sighs]

696
00:36:20,429 --> 00:36:22,597
Hey, what are you doing here?

697
00:36:22,598 --> 00:36:23,849
I need to tell you something.

698
00:36:25,142 --> 00:36:26,350
No, that's fine.

699
00:36:26,351 --> 00:36:27,853
You haven't eaten yet, have you?

700
00:36:28,437 --> 00:36:29,855
Drink this while you wait.

701
00:36:48,123 --> 00:36:49,248
[sighs]

702
00:36:49,249 --> 00:36:50,459
[cell phone vibrating]

703
00:36:55,672 --> 00:36:56,882
MANAGER KIM DONG-SEOK

704
00:36:58,842 --> 00:37:00,384
I told you not to call.

705
00:37:00,385 --> 00:37:03,346
I called to apologize.
Let's talk face-to-face.

706
00:37:03,347 --> 00:37:05,098
Should I come to Bansang-dong now?

707
00:37:06,099 --> 00:37:08,017
How do you know I'm in Bansang-dong?

708
00:37:08,018 --> 00:37:10,395
Uh... I heard it from Eun-ha.

709
00:37:11,980 --> 00:37:13,272
I'm hanging up.

710
00:37:13,273 --> 00:37:14,357
[line disconnects]

711
00:37:14,358 --> 00:37:16,150
[footsteps approaching]

712
00:37:16,151 --> 00:37:17,526
[Sun-woo sighs]

713
00:37:17,527 --> 00:37:20,697
Sweet red bean, cheese, custard cream.
Pick whichever you like.

714
00:37:29,998 --> 00:37:31,375
[gentle music playing]

715
00:37:52,562 --> 00:37:54,480
About that vehicle fire,

716
00:37:54,481 --> 00:37:56,524
I discovered a lead
that might help the case.

717
00:37:56,525 --> 00:38:00,070
If you give me just one more chance,
I'll tell you what it is.

718
00:38:01,530 --> 00:38:04,533
How much is all this?
This should cover it, right?

719
00:38:08,578 --> 00:38:11,580
- [sighs]
- Oh. Let me just say one thing.

720
00:38:11,581 --> 00:38:14,042
Whatever you do,
you must never resort to tricks.

721
00:38:14,710 --> 00:38:16,877
Especially at work,
character and reputation

722
00:38:16,878 --> 00:38:18,505
matter more than work competence.

723
00:38:19,339 --> 00:38:21,257
But once those go wrong,

724
00:38:21,258 --> 00:38:23,677
that label can follow you around
for decades.

725
00:38:24,261 --> 00:38:25,761
Im Eun-ha in Legal Affairs
was a classmate.

726
00:38:25,762 --> 00:38:28,180
I ran into her
after I failed the interview.

727
00:38:28,181 --> 00:38:31,308
I heard about this while
we were talking, and I found this online.

728
00:38:31,309 --> 00:38:32,811
CHRONIC MOTORS FIRE VICTIM
"IT WAS PURE HELL"

729
00:38:34,062 --> 00:38:36,523
What is it that you want to say?

730
00:38:39,192 --> 00:38:40,985
I was the one who made this bracelet.

731
00:38:40,986 --> 00:38:43,446
The stones are hard to get,
imported from Italy,

732
00:38:43,447 --> 00:38:46,032
and quite expensive,
so I remember it, trust me.

733
00:38:46,033 --> 00:38:49,453
Because of this scar on my arm,
I can't even wear short sleeves anymore.

734
00:38:51,329 --> 00:38:54,081
Well, that day,
this man bought three in total.

735
00:38:54,082 --> 00:38:56,959
One men's bracelet and two women's.

736
00:38:56,960 --> 00:38:58,294
There were two delivery addresses.

737
00:38:58,295 --> 00:39:01,548
Here in Bansang-dong, and Muneun-dong.

738
00:39:02,632 --> 00:39:03,467
Muneun-dong?

739
00:39:04,718 --> 00:39:07,845
If you look at the order records,
the women's bracelets are different sizes.

740
00:39:07,846 --> 00:39:11,807
Nine times out of ten, someone who orders
couples' bracelets in this way

741
00:39:11,808 --> 00:39:13,226
is having an affair.

742
00:39:18,106 --> 00:39:19,690
Causes of vehicle fires

743
00:39:19,691 --> 00:39:22,818
include excessive modifications,
major collisions,

744
00:39:22,819 --> 00:39:25,237
flammable materials left in the car,
and flooding.

745
00:39:25,238 --> 00:39:26,822
In the CCTV footage on the news,

746
00:39:26,823 --> 00:39:28,908
smoke started when
she turned the car on remotely.

747
00:39:28,909 --> 00:39:32,495
Given the circumstances,
an electrical short is highly likely.

748
00:39:32,496 --> 00:39:34,330
- So what?
- Look, when a car is flooded,

749
00:39:34,331 --> 00:39:37,374
the wiring and relay contacts
can cause a short circuit.

750
00:39:37,375 --> 00:39:38,542
That can lead to a fire.

751
00:39:38,543 --> 00:39:40,169
And during the last heavy rain,

752
00:39:40,170 --> 00:39:42,588
the place where the news
reported flood damage

753
00:39:42,589 --> 00:39:44,381
is at that address in Muneun-dong.

754
00:39:44,382 --> 00:39:46,259
DELIVERY ADDRESS 2
MUNEUN-DONG, CHEONGUN-GU, SEOUL

755
00:39:48,345 --> 00:39:50,097
Did you ask Ms. Im Eun-ha about that too?

756
00:39:50,680 --> 00:39:53,474
No. I've never taken
anything that far before.

757
00:39:53,475 --> 00:39:56,602
If you came here to do something
you've never done before,

758
00:39:56,603 --> 00:39:59,063
then you should've made an effort
you've never made before.

759
00:39:59,064 --> 00:40:03,025
Actually, this is the first time
I've even heard of "relay contacts."

760
00:40:03,026 --> 00:40:05,820
Anyway, since neither his home
or his workplace flooded,

761
00:40:05,821 --> 00:40:08,406
that means there's only one place
left to check.

762
00:40:09,407 --> 00:40:13,662
So you want to trade
the Muneun-dong address for an internship?

763
00:40:14,996 --> 00:40:16,331
That was my plan,

764
00:40:17,124 --> 00:40:18,999
but why don't I just tell you.

765
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:22,212
And the way that you stuck
to your principles, that was pretty cool.

766
00:40:24,422 --> 00:40:26,675
Have you switched
your strategy to flattery?

767
00:40:27,384 --> 00:40:29,927
Never mind. Just give me
the Muneun-dong address.

768
00:40:29,928 --> 00:40:31,221
[Han-su] Here.

769
00:40:37,644 --> 00:40:39,270
You remember me, right?

770
00:40:39,271 --> 00:40:41,313
I'm Kang Yi-ji from
Chronic Motors' Legal Affairs.

771
00:40:41,314 --> 00:40:43,942
We're supposed to meet
the day after tomorrow.

772
00:40:44,734 --> 00:40:46,486
And I'll only speak with Mr. Jung Ki-tae.

773
00:40:47,070 --> 00:40:49,364
[Yi-ji] We've uncovered
some new information.

774
00:40:50,407 --> 00:40:51,991
Would it be all right with you?

775
00:40:51,992 --> 00:40:54,536
What is it this time?
Please, just stop it.

776
00:40:58,498 --> 00:41:01,917
Something like this is as painful
emotionally as it is physically.

777
00:41:01,918 --> 00:41:05,379
We want to solve this situation for you,
but you gotta help us a little.

778
00:41:05,380 --> 00:41:06,339
[sighs]

779
00:41:07,841 --> 00:41:11,303
Wow, that bracelet is beautiful.
You wear it even in the hospital?

780
00:41:11,928 --> 00:41:13,804
[So-yeong] My husband had it custom-made.

781
00:41:13,805 --> 00:41:16,016
There's only one pair in the whole world.

782
00:41:16,683 --> 00:41:19,686
I think it would look prettier
with the clasp on the other side.

783
00:41:20,353 --> 00:41:21,938
Can I try it?

784
00:41:31,156 --> 00:41:33,074
- Ah!
- [So-yeong gasps]

785
00:41:33,783 --> 00:41:35,410
So I can wear it this way too.

786
00:41:36,328 --> 00:41:38,496
The cloud-shaped charm is double-sided.

787
00:41:38,955 --> 00:41:40,789
[So-yeong] How did you know that?

788
00:41:40,790 --> 00:41:41,791
Goodness!

789
00:41:46,880 --> 00:41:50,258
[clears throat]
Then let's just talk for five minutes.

790
00:41:55,180 --> 00:41:57,641
I mean, why are you showing me this?

791
00:41:58,850 --> 00:42:01,685
When the Muneun-dong area
flooded in the heavy rain,

792
00:42:01,686 --> 00:42:05,523
the building management clearly remembered
rushing to get your car out in time.

793
00:42:06,233 --> 00:42:07,233
So what?

794
00:42:07,234 --> 00:42:09,319
Do all flooded cars catch fire?

795
00:42:10,278 --> 00:42:14,573
As you already said, a car being flooded
doesn't necessarily cause a fire.

796
00:42:14,574 --> 00:42:17,201
But when unauthorized,
illegal modifications

797
00:42:17,202 --> 00:42:18,827
are added to the equation,

798
00:42:18,828 --> 00:42:21,163
flooding can corrode
the connectors or wiring,

799
00:42:21,164 --> 00:42:25,251
making it more likely that an electrical
short will occur and lead to a fire.

800
00:42:25,252 --> 00:42:27,253
What are you talking about?

801
00:42:27,254 --> 00:42:31,382
I'm afraid there was one other thing
you hid from us besides the flooding.

802
00:42:31,383 --> 00:42:33,884
- The ballet academy.
- Wha... what?

803
00:42:33,885 --> 00:42:36,929
You have only two sons,
but you recently visited a ballet academy.

804
00:42:36,930 --> 00:42:38,639
- My card.
- [Yi-ji] <i>Right next door</i>

805
00:42:38,640 --> 00:42:40,641
<i>is a private auto repair shop
without a sign</i>

806
00:42:40,642 --> 00:42:43,061
that doesn't even show up
in Internet searches.

807
00:42:44,145 --> 00:42:46,605
When you had remote start
installed in 2022,

808
00:42:46,606 --> 00:42:48,816
you altered all the factory wiring,
didn't you?

809
00:42:48,817 --> 00:42:50,317
And when the car flooded last week,

810
00:42:50,318 --> 00:42:52,778
you went back to have
the corrosion cleaned off.

811
00:42:52,779 --> 00:42:54,405
[grunts] That was--

812
00:42:54,406 --> 00:42:57,241
And you even looked into
selling it overseas in that condition.

813
00:42:57,242 --> 00:43:00,119
That means you knew very well
that it wouldn't be strange

814
00:43:00,120 --> 00:43:01,997
if the car blew up at any given moment.

815
00:43:03,248 --> 00:43:07,544
And your wife, who wasn't aware,
was the one who started it that day.

816
00:43:10,255 --> 00:43:11,965
The results aren't out yet.

817
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:13,966
They will be soon.

818
00:43:13,967 --> 00:43:17,344
But unfortunately, there will be
hardly any other options left

819
00:43:17,345 --> 00:43:19,431
for you to choose from by then.

820
00:43:20,348 --> 00:43:23,184
Uh, also, your wife has no idea

821
00:43:23,768 --> 00:43:27,230
that the flooding we're talking about
happened in Muneun-dong.

822
00:43:28,815 --> 00:43:31,650
Is this the attitude of someone
who's here to negotiate?

823
00:43:31,651 --> 00:43:33,444
If you're going to act like this,

824
00:43:33,445 --> 00:43:34,862
I won't stand for it.

825
00:43:34,863 --> 00:43:37,324
I'll post online
and we'll take it to court.

826
00:43:38,325 --> 00:43:39,491
If things escalate that far,

827
00:43:39,492 --> 00:43:43,371
the company will have no choice
but to disclose all the evidence.

828
00:43:44,831 --> 00:43:46,166
[Han-su] All the evidence?

829
00:43:47,417 --> 00:43:48,792
That would include

830
00:43:48,793 --> 00:43:51,880
these photos I have here
of the flooding in Muneun-dong.

831
00:43:53,673 --> 00:43:57,968
For now, bringing this case to a close
as quickly as possible

832
00:43:57,969 --> 00:44:01,306
would be the best option
for both you and the company.

833
00:44:02,349 --> 00:44:04,059
You need to protect your family.

834
00:44:11,274 --> 00:44:12,650
Ah, I don't need this.

835
00:44:13,818 --> 00:44:15,486
Uh, how about we do this?

836
00:44:15,487 --> 00:44:17,488
It's not you paying me money.

837
00:44:17,489 --> 00:44:20,449
It's just you getting me
the compensation amount.

838
00:44:20,450 --> 00:44:24,329
I'll give you the cut of 50%.
It'll stay between the two of us. Huh?

839
00:44:28,625 --> 00:44:30,209
Would you like to keep talking?

840
00:44:30,210 --> 00:44:32,212
[sighs in exasperation]

841
00:44:34,464 --> 00:44:36,341
[suspenseful music playing]

842
00:44:58,029 --> 00:45:00,072
[intriguing music playing]

843
00:45:00,073 --> 00:45:01,449
[Sun-woo] Huh?

844
00:45:02,117 --> 00:45:02,992
What?

845
00:45:07,497 --> 00:45:08,665
[chuckles]

846
00:45:09,499 --> 00:45:11,209
Do you want to eat some more?

847
00:45:12,502 --> 00:45:14,129
Mr. Park Geon-woo.

848
00:45:17,966 --> 00:45:19,134
[sighs]

849
00:45:22,512 --> 00:45:23,846
[sighs]

850
00:45:23,847 --> 00:45:25,682
What? Why?

851
00:45:26,307 --> 00:45:29,977
[sighs] I don't have the energy to run,
or any money to pay you back.

852
00:45:29,978 --> 00:45:30,937
Do your worst!

853
00:45:31,521 --> 00:45:34,565
[scoffs] Shouldn't you try
just saying sorry first?

854
00:45:34,566 --> 00:45:36,066
[Mi-jin] I'm sorry!

855
00:45:36,067 --> 00:45:38,611
But with him that sick,
I couldn't think things through.

856
00:45:39,737 --> 00:45:40,864
I can see that.

857
00:45:41,573 --> 00:45:44,867
But why lie about studying abroad?
Was I that bad to be with?

858
00:45:44,868 --> 00:45:46,410
[Mi-jin] You gave me more than enough.

859
00:45:46,411 --> 00:45:49,122
That's why I did it.
So you'd hate me and cut ties.

860
00:45:49,956 --> 00:45:51,415
- What?
- If I'd told you the truth,

861
00:45:51,416 --> 00:45:53,625
you would've done anything to fix it.

862
00:45:53,626 --> 00:45:55,419
Rather than that, I thought I'd betray you

863
00:45:55,420 --> 00:45:57,087
and make a clean break
from your life. What?

864
00:45:57,088 --> 00:45:58,213
Nah, you really--

865
00:45:58,214 --> 00:46:00,090
Whether it's showing loyalty
or being a burden,

866
00:46:00,091 --> 00:46:02,135
there's a limit. It's terrible to do.

867
00:46:03,386 --> 00:46:05,430
You're far too well-meaning
for your own good.

868
00:46:06,055 --> 00:46:08,558
- That's not for you to say.
- Exactly.

869
00:46:09,434 --> 00:46:11,478
[soft music playing]

870
00:46:16,316 --> 00:46:18,443
I really appreciate your help today.

871
00:46:21,070 --> 00:46:22,322
But why the long face?

872
00:46:22,655 --> 00:46:26,116
[sighing] Is it really right
to cover up his affair like this?

873
00:46:26,117 --> 00:46:28,076
I feel so sorry for his wife.

874
00:46:28,077 --> 00:46:30,204
She's a homemaker with two sons.

875
00:46:30,205 --> 00:46:32,080
An apartment worth billions of won,

876
00:46:32,081 --> 00:46:33,957
an expensive
English-language kindergarten,

877
00:46:33,958 --> 00:46:35,542
overseas trips every quarter.

878
00:46:35,543 --> 00:46:38,253
All the assets and expenses
come from her husband.

879
00:46:38,254 --> 00:46:40,088
Only the couple knows
their own circumstances.

880
00:46:40,089 --> 00:46:42,758
- We have no right to interfere.
- She has a right to be respected.

881
00:46:42,759 --> 00:46:44,510
His wife has a right to know as well.

882
00:46:44,511 --> 00:46:46,595
She might already know.

883
00:46:46,596 --> 00:46:49,806
She may be using this incident
to make her husband feel guilty

884
00:46:49,807 --> 00:46:52,018
and gain the upper hand in their marriage.

885
00:46:52,644 --> 00:46:54,394
How do you even come up with that?

886
00:46:54,395 --> 00:46:57,398
Let's just say
I analyzed the possibilities.

887
00:46:59,025 --> 00:46:59,984
Hmm.

888
00:47:01,736 --> 00:47:02,986
You worked hard today.

889
00:47:02,987 --> 00:47:04,905
Let's work together
for three months to start.

890
00:47:04,906 --> 00:47:06,658
[sighs] All right.

891
00:47:08,368 --> 00:47:09,702
What?!

892
00:47:12,372 --> 00:47:14,123
[door opens]

893
00:47:15,333 --> 00:47:16,960
- Hey, you're back.
- [sighs]

894
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:24,842
[blows]

895
00:47:25,301 --> 00:47:27,302
[Sun-woo]
Notice anything different about me?

896
00:47:27,303 --> 00:47:29,889
Did you buy clothes? Get your hair done?

897
00:47:31,266 --> 00:47:33,016
You went and ate something alone,
didn't you?

898
00:47:33,017 --> 00:47:35,769
- What have I done more recently?
- Recently?

899
00:47:35,770 --> 00:47:37,604
What have you done recently?

900
00:47:37,605 --> 00:47:38,730
Oh, right.

901
00:47:38,731 --> 00:47:40,775
Your interview at Chronic Motors.

902
00:47:41,526 --> 00:47:42,818
Let's go for a drink
to drown your sorrows.

903
00:47:42,819 --> 00:47:44,820
No. I got a position!

904
00:47:44,821 --> 00:47:46,906
- Let's celebrate!
- Huh?

905
00:47:47,490 --> 00:47:48,490
Really?

906
00:47:48,491 --> 00:47:51,243
- Wow, that's amazing! Damn!
- Hey, don't get carried away.

907
00:47:51,244 --> 00:47:53,662
- It's a three-month internship.
- Hey, that's still something.

908
00:47:53,663 --> 00:47:55,081
You're guaranteed 90 days.

909
00:47:55,873 --> 00:47:58,625
Oh, I've got good news too.

910
00:47:58,626 --> 00:47:59,919
[Sun-woo] What is it?

911
00:48:00,920 --> 00:48:02,589
- I found us a place.
- Already?

912
00:48:03,756 --> 00:48:06,633
[sighs] We only had until
the end of the month, didn't we?

913
00:48:06,634 --> 00:48:09,720
[scoffs] I told you to not get
your panties in a bunch, seriously!

914
00:48:09,721 --> 00:48:12,806
Hey, take a proper look.
Right in the middle of Seoul.

915
00:48:12,807 --> 00:48:14,058
Very fancy.

916
00:48:14,642 --> 00:48:17,144
My cousin suddenly got transferred
to the US, so I begged him.

917
00:48:17,145 --> 00:48:18,687
I looked after the place as an excuse.

918
00:48:18,688 --> 00:48:20,063
But won't the maintenance fee be bad?

919
00:48:20,064 --> 00:48:22,232
It's a ten-minute commute by bike
to Chronic Motors,

920
00:48:22,233 --> 00:48:23,775
so you won't waste time or money
on the road.

921
00:48:23,776 --> 00:48:25,027
You're gonna sleep more,

922
00:48:25,028 --> 00:48:27,447
and even your happiness level
is gonna go up.

923
00:48:29,240 --> 00:48:30,949
Okay, I'm in.

924
00:48:30,950 --> 00:48:33,660
But two of the rooms
are full of my cousin's things,

925
00:48:33,661 --> 00:48:35,579
so there's only one bedroom.

926
00:48:35,580 --> 00:48:36,663
You can take it.

927
00:48:36,664 --> 00:48:38,790
Oh, come on. You take the bedroom.

928
00:48:38,791 --> 00:48:42,169
I'll stick to the living room
so it'll be easier for you to work.

929
00:48:42,170 --> 00:48:44,254
Hey, you don't have to do that.

930
00:48:44,255 --> 00:48:45,505
Thanks, brother.

931
00:48:45,506 --> 00:48:47,132
- Just a "thank you"?
- Then what?

932
00:48:47,133 --> 00:48:48,258
I'm gonna get fried chicken.

933
00:48:48,259 --> 00:48:49,885
- Hey, bro. Give it here.
- Hey, don't get close.

934
00:48:49,886 --> 00:48:51,803
- Seriously. I'll hurt you.
- Please, I'll order it.

935
00:48:51,804 --> 00:48:53,640
- Come on.
- Don't. I'll drop your phone in.

936
00:49:07,654 --> 00:49:09,446
[Kyung-shim] <i>There's soup in the fridge.</i>

937
00:49:09,447 --> 00:49:10,781
<i>Heat it up and eat it.</i>

938
00:49:10,782 --> 00:49:12,575
<i>I threw out all the instant food.</i>

939
00:49:21,918 --> 00:49:23,586
[cell phone vibrating]

940
00:49:27,882 --> 00:49:32,094
Mom, I told you not to come over
whenever you want.

941
00:49:32,095 --> 00:49:36,139
And what's with the laundry?
Don't throw my things away without asking.

942
00:49:36,140 --> 00:49:38,684
[Kyung-shim] <i>If you let laundry pile up,
good luck will leave you.</i>

943
00:49:38,685 --> 00:49:40,769
<i>Bring the soup in the fridge
to a good boil and eat it.</i>

944
00:49:40,770 --> 00:49:41,853
Just, please--

945
00:49:41,854 --> 00:49:43,397
<i>Dong-seok proposed, didn't he?</i>

946
00:49:43,398 --> 00:49:46,191
<i>I saw the pictures
of your new home. It looks nice.</i>

947
00:49:46,192 --> 00:49:48,360
He sent you pictures?

948
00:49:48,361 --> 00:49:51,154
<i>Hey, isn't it wonderful of him
to be so thoughtful even with me?</i>

949
00:49:51,155 --> 00:49:53,865
Oh, Mom, that's just being creepy.

950
00:49:53,866 --> 00:49:55,909
<i>I have nothing left to worry about now.</i>

951
00:49:55,910 --> 00:49:58,495
<i>I could die right now with no regrets.</i>

952
00:49:58,496 --> 00:50:00,288
[scoffs] Why would you say that?

953
00:50:00,289 --> 00:50:01,915
<i>Stop by the house.</i>

954
00:50:01,916 --> 00:50:05,293
<i>I'll show you the information
about that wedding fair I mentioned.</i>

955
00:50:05,294 --> 00:50:08,630
Let's talk later. I'm so tired right now.

956
00:50:08,631 --> 00:50:12,092
- Get some rest.
<i>- Hey, hey! I still have more to say.</i>

957
00:50:12,093 --> 00:50:13,136
[line disconnects]

958
00:50:14,303 --> 00:50:15,930
8 MISSED CALLS
MANAGER KIM DONG-SEOK

959
00:50:25,940 --> 00:50:28,234
[gentle music playing]

960
00:50:55,970 --> 00:50:58,765
The Rosette Nebula?
It was actually photographed!

961
00:51:04,228 --> 00:51:05,646
[gentle music swells]

962
00:51:06,731 --> 00:51:07,732
[gasps]

963
00:51:34,342 --> 00:51:35,468
Beautiful!

964
00:51:39,222 --> 00:51:40,640
[suspenseful music playing]

965
00:51:41,808 --> 00:51:43,142
[keyboard clacking]

966
00:51:44,185 --> 00:51:46,436
CHRONIC MOTORS EMPLOYEE
THREATENS FIRE VICTIM

967
00:51:46,437 --> 00:51:47,730
POST

968
00:51:48,564 --> 00:51:50,190
CHRONIC MOTORS
VICTIMS' GROUP

969
00:51:50,191 --> 00:51:51,734
WE'RE SPEAKING OUT

970
00:51:52,485 --> 00:51:54,319
THE WOMAN IN THE VIDEO
WORKS FOR CHRONIC MOTORS

971
00:51:54,320 --> 00:51:56,947
SHE EVEN CAME TO THE HOSPITAL
TO SILENCE THE CAR OWNER

972
00:51:56,948 --> 00:51:58,449
IS BRAND IMAGE
WORTH MORE THAN HUMAN LIFE?

973
00:51:59,158 --> 00:52:01,618
[male protestor]
We need answers about the fire!

974
00:52:01,619 --> 00:52:03,453
[protestors] Explain it! Explain it!

975
00:52:03,454 --> 00:52:05,497
[male protestor]
Transparency! Transparency!

976
00:52:05,498 --> 00:52:07,207
[protestors] Explain it! Explain it!

977
00:52:07,208 --> 00:52:09,877
[male protestor]
Transparency! Transparency!

978
00:52:35,736 --> 00:52:38,447
[uplifting music playing]

979
00:52:39,949 --> 00:52:41,200
[exhales heavily]

980
00:52:43,369 --> 00:52:44,203
[beeps]

981
00:52:47,707 --> 00:52:49,500
Yeah. Mm, get off.

982
00:52:50,376 --> 00:52:53,044
Since this is your first office job,
let me tell you.

983
00:52:53,045 --> 00:52:55,881
Greeting everyone you run into
at work is a must here.

984
00:52:55,882 --> 00:52:57,674
You're the bottom rung of the ladder.

985
00:52:57,675 --> 00:52:59,885
Hello. I'm Han Sun-woo, intern.

986
00:52:59,886 --> 00:53:01,428
This is the break room.

987
00:53:01,429 --> 00:53:03,054
[sighs] I'm ready to greet

988
00:53:03,055 --> 00:53:05,641
even the potted plants
in the hallway today, so don't worry.

989
00:53:06,225 --> 00:53:08,059
Hello. I'm Han Sun-woo, the intern.

990
00:53:08,060 --> 00:53:09,895
Oh, you're doing great.

991
00:53:09,896 --> 00:53:11,147
Whoo!

992
00:53:11,772 --> 00:53:12,732
All right.

993
00:53:14,901 --> 00:53:16,569
This is the Legal Affairs.

994
00:53:17,361 --> 00:53:19,487
This is the meeting room.

995
00:53:19,488 --> 00:53:21,656
Mmm. There are CCTVs,

996
00:53:21,657 --> 00:53:23,366
and they pick up sound
better than you'd think,

997
00:53:23,367 --> 00:53:24,659
so watch what you say.

998
00:53:24,660 --> 00:53:26,578
Uh, if you want to swear,
go to the break room.

999
00:53:26,579 --> 00:53:28,330
There's a blind spot
in front of the coffee machine.

1000
00:53:28,331 --> 00:53:30,916
And if you want to cry,
the bathroom is the safest.

1001
00:53:30,917 --> 00:53:33,543
I don't think I'll have any reason
to swear or cry.

1002
00:53:33,544 --> 00:53:35,212
I thought that at first, too.

1003
00:53:36,255 --> 00:53:37,840
[Sun-woo chuckles]

1004
00:53:39,008 --> 00:53:40,800
This is our intern, Han Sun-woo.

1005
00:53:40,801 --> 00:53:44,346
Hello, I'm Han Sun-woo, the intern.
I look forward to working with you.

1006
00:53:44,347 --> 00:53:46,306
- We look forward to working with you, too.
- Right.

1007
00:53:46,307 --> 00:53:47,642
This is your desk.

1008
00:53:48,309 --> 00:53:51,019
Don't go overboard decorating it
while you're a newbie.

1009
00:53:51,020 --> 00:53:53,647
It could make you look
kinda silly to the bosses.

1010
00:53:53,648 --> 00:53:55,399
- Where's your desk?
- Right here.

1011
00:53:57,485 --> 00:53:58,903
[chuckles]

1012
00:54:00,988 --> 00:54:03,448
You and Ms. Kang were amazing, though.

1013
00:54:03,449 --> 00:54:06,952
[sighs] I hope this gets her promoted
to general manager quickly.

1014
00:54:06,953 --> 00:54:10,914
[gasps] Did you see
Mr. Kim Dong-seok's post?

1015
00:54:10,915 --> 00:54:12,750
- [band plays over phone]
- [gasps]

1016
00:54:14,877 --> 00:54:18,046
Oh, wow. I guess
proposals like this are still possible.

1017
00:54:18,047 --> 00:54:20,841
Wow, that's so classic.

1018
00:54:21,509 --> 00:54:23,177
But this isn't her style.

1019
00:54:25,972 --> 00:54:27,515
Stop, stop watching it.

1020
00:54:30,476 --> 00:54:32,228
AGREEMENT NOT TO SUE
AND WAIVER OF CLAIMS

1021
00:54:34,271 --> 00:54:36,857
Don't let your guard down.
Not until it's stamped.

1022
00:54:37,483 --> 00:54:40,319
Yes. I'll see you later
with the settlement agreement.

1023
00:54:43,531 --> 00:54:47,284
I hear you resolved it, ma'am.
You're good.

1024
00:54:48,077 --> 00:54:50,537
But is that the end of it?

1025
00:54:50,538 --> 00:54:52,372
Don't let your guard down.

1026
00:54:52,373 --> 00:54:55,001
People outside might see it differently.

1027
00:54:55,835 --> 00:54:59,379
Oh, and I hear there's something else
to congratulate you on.

1028
00:54:59,380 --> 00:55:01,132
You've got many things to celebrate.

1029
00:55:07,722 --> 00:55:10,432
Uh, Ms. Kang, have you seen the video?

1030
00:55:10,433 --> 00:55:12,434
What video are you talking about?

1031
00:55:12,435 --> 00:55:16,689
Oh, Mr. Kim posted the proposal video,
and everyone's talking about it.

1032
00:55:17,732 --> 00:55:19,025
[somber music playing]

1033
00:55:23,988 --> 00:55:27,407
The car owner is coming this afternoon,
so please review the settlement agreement.

1034
00:55:27,408 --> 00:55:28,701
Okay.

1035
00:55:32,163 --> 00:55:33,831
[door closes]

1036
00:55:38,252 --> 00:55:39,295
[knock on door]

1037
00:55:40,337 --> 00:55:41,338
Yes?

1038
00:55:44,175 --> 00:55:46,634
- [door closes]
- What do you have for me?

1039
00:55:46,635 --> 00:55:47,803
Your mail.

1040
00:55:52,475 --> 00:55:54,310
You're in a tough spot, aren't you?

1041
00:55:54,935 --> 00:55:58,188
It's your first day at your first job,
and you're asking me that?

1042
00:55:58,189 --> 00:56:01,525
Distributing video of someone's
private life without consent...

1043
00:56:04,820 --> 00:56:08,115
[sighs] If there's anything I can do
to help, please let me know.

1044
00:56:10,868 --> 00:56:14,579
For today, look through the shared files
and familiarize yourself.

1045
00:56:14,580 --> 00:56:15,748
Yes.

1046
00:56:22,213 --> 00:56:23,713
You don't answer my calls.

1047
00:56:23,714 --> 00:56:25,298
Now, I finally get to see you.

1048
00:56:25,299 --> 00:56:27,801
We've broken up.
Why would I answer your calls?

1049
00:56:27,802 --> 00:56:28,969
[scoffs]

1050
00:56:30,638 --> 00:56:32,556
Just marry me already. Hmm?

1051
00:56:33,140 --> 00:56:36,184
I even took out a loan and signed
for the house. Isn't that enough?

1052
00:56:36,185 --> 00:56:37,686
The house is in your name.

1053
00:56:38,604 --> 00:56:40,105
Take the video down right now,

1054
00:56:40,106 --> 00:56:42,566
and don't ever contact my mom again.

1055
00:56:44,110 --> 00:56:48,989
[sighs] Kang Yi-ji,
don't take this any further.

1056
00:56:50,074 --> 00:56:51,533
You will regret it.

1057
00:56:51,534 --> 00:56:53,326
I won't regret anything.

1058
00:56:53,327 --> 00:56:55,870
I'm telling you for the last time.

1059
00:56:55,871 --> 00:56:58,331
I have no intention of seeing you again.

1060
00:56:58,332 --> 00:56:59,707
[knock on door]

1061
00:56:59,708 --> 00:57:01,209
[door opens]

1062
00:57:01,210 --> 00:57:03,254
Ms. Kang, the car owner is here.

1063
00:57:03,921 --> 00:57:06,090
Go on. We'll talk later.

1064
00:57:10,052 --> 00:57:11,719
[door closes]

1065
00:57:11,720 --> 00:57:13,680
[Yi-ji] Please read it carefully.

1066
00:57:13,681 --> 00:57:15,765
The key point of this settlement agreement
is the non-litigation clause.

1067
00:57:15,766 --> 00:57:17,058
CONFIRMATION OF THE CAUSE OF THE ACCIDENT

1068
00:57:17,059 --> 00:57:19,269
By acknowledging
the illegal modifications,

1069
00:57:19,270 --> 00:57:23,565
you are promising not to bring any civil
or criminal proceedings in the future.

1070
00:57:23,566 --> 00:57:25,608
On the condition that the case is closed,

1071
00:57:25,609 --> 00:57:29,279
we have also offered the maximum
goodwill compensation we can provide.

1072
00:57:29,280 --> 00:57:30,614
[Han-su] Never mind that.

1073
00:57:31,532 --> 00:57:34,326
Delete those photos
and the recording right away.

1074
00:57:36,036 --> 00:57:38,037
They'd be of no use to us,
even if we kept them.

1075
00:57:38,038 --> 00:57:39,414
VICTIM'S REPRESENTATIVE
NAME: JIN HAN-SU

1076
00:57:39,415 --> 00:57:41,791
[male protestor]
Transparency! Transparency!

1077
00:57:41,792 --> 00:57:44,669
Have a safe trip back,
and please come to us when you need us.

1078
00:57:44,670 --> 00:57:47,046
I have no reason to come back here.

1079
00:57:47,047 --> 00:57:49,215
[man 1] Look there!
There, there! He's out.

1080
00:57:49,216 --> 00:57:50,633
[woman] Oh, oh, oh, oh!

1081
00:57:50,634 --> 00:57:52,677
- [man 1] Come on. Look, look.
- Quick, quick.

1082
00:57:52,678 --> 00:57:54,846
Sir, did you really reach a settlement?

1083
00:57:54,847 --> 00:57:57,473
[man 2] Why would you settle?
Just sue them!

1084
00:57:57,474 --> 00:57:58,433
[man 1] Yeah!

1085
00:57:58,434 --> 00:58:00,476
Luckily, we've resolved
the matter amicably.

1086
00:58:00,477 --> 00:58:02,187
[woman] Amicably, my ass!

1087
00:58:02,188 --> 00:58:04,772
All you big corporations know
is how to abuse power.

1088
00:58:04,773 --> 00:58:06,858
That's her!
She's the woman in the video, isn't she?

1089
00:58:06,859 --> 00:58:09,652
- [man 3] Yeah, that's her!
- Yes, she is. This is her.

1090
00:58:09,653 --> 00:58:10,570
There she is!

1091
00:58:10,571 --> 00:58:12,906
Now you're threatening people
with their family?

1092
00:58:12,907 --> 00:58:14,824
Please tell them that it's not true.

1093
00:58:14,825 --> 00:58:17,285
I signed the settlement agreement,

1094
00:58:17,286 --> 00:58:19,954
but there wasn't a clause saying
I had to explain things like this to you.

1095
00:58:19,955 --> 00:58:22,999
I'm sick to death of you and your company.

1096
00:58:23,000 --> 00:58:26,544
Yes. You know better than anyone
whether you threatened me or not!

1097
00:58:26,545 --> 00:58:29,005
- [man 1] Yes, that's right.
- [man 2] She definitely threatened him.

1098
00:58:29,006 --> 00:58:30,089
[man 3] She threatened him.

1099
00:58:30,090 --> 00:58:32,717
- [woman] We want refunds for all of us.
- It's a fraud.

1100
00:58:32,718 --> 00:58:34,052
[all clamoring]

1101
00:58:34,053 --> 00:58:35,762
You must not act recklessly like this.

1102
00:58:35,763 --> 00:58:37,597
- Hey, give us a refund!
- [gasps]

1103
00:58:37,598 --> 00:58:39,141
[voices echoing]

1104
00:58:40,267 --> 00:58:42,353
[faint clamoring]

1105
00:58:45,356 --> 00:58:46,565
[tense music playing]

1106
00:58:49,443 --> 00:58:50,527
[man] It's a fraud!

1107
00:58:58,118 --> 00:59:00,119
[theme song playing]

1108
00:59:00,120 --> 00:59:02,289
[imperceptible]

1109
00:59:03,582 --> 00:59:06,794
[singer vocalizing]

1110
00:59:14,301 --> 00:59:16,219
<i>♪ Didn't see it coming ♪</i>

1111
00:59:16,220 --> 00:59:17,845
<i>♪ I didn't hear a sound ♪</i>

1112
00:59:17,846 --> 00:59:19,514
<i>♪ I wasn't even searching ♪</i>

1113
00:59:19,515 --> 00:59:21,349
<i>♪ Crashed into my life ♪</i>

1114
00:59:21,350 --> 00:59:23,393
<i>♪ The air feels different ♪</i>

1115
00:59:23,394 --> 00:59:25,353
<i>♪ When you're in the room ♪</i>

1116
00:59:25,354 --> 00:59:27,021
<i>♪ If the world goes quiet ♪</i>

1117
00:59:27,022 --> 00:59:28,731
<i>♪ It's just me and you ♪</i>

1118
00:59:28,732 --> 00:59:30,149
<i>♪ Don't need a reason ♪</i>

1119
00:59:30,150 --> 00:59:32,527
<i>♪ Don't need a cause ♪</i>

1120
00:59:32,528 --> 00:59:35,863
<i>♪ Don't need four seasons
Or a round of applause ♪</i>

1121
00:59:35,864 --> 00:59:37,282
<i>♪ It's you ♪</i>

1122
00:59:37,283 --> 00:59:39,158
<i>♪ Just us ♪</i>

1123
00:59:39,159 --> 00:59:41,327
<i>♪ Just this ♪</i>

1124
00:59:41,328 --> 00:59:42,787
<i>♪ Just 'cause ♪</i>

1125
00:59:42,788 --> 00:59:44,872
Yeah. I spent a lot of money.

1126
00:59:44,873 --> 00:59:45,832
EPILOGUE

1127
00:59:45,833 --> 00:59:47,667
Yeah. The ring, the flowers.

1128
00:59:47,668 --> 00:59:49,961
Hey, why are flowers
so expensive these days?

1129
00:59:49,962 --> 00:59:50,879
Huh? Hold on.

1130
00:59:53,382 --> 00:59:54,925
Oh!

1131
00:59:55,676 --> 00:59:58,261
Do you think it's easy
to land a wife with a good career?

1132
00:59:58,262 --> 01:00:00,972
I mean, if I propose
where there are lots of people,

1133
01:00:00,973 --> 01:00:02,599
do you think she can say no?

1134
01:00:03,309 --> 01:00:05,018
[sighs] Don't even get me started.

1135
01:00:05,019 --> 01:00:07,812
I went to her mother's house
and changed everything myself.

1136
01:00:07,813 --> 01:00:10,523
The bathroom tap, the fixtures,
even the light bulbs.

1137
01:00:10,524 --> 01:00:12,233
I'll call you back, yeah?

1138
01:00:12,234 --> 01:00:13,693
Oh, hello.

1139
01:00:13,694 --> 01:00:15,737
Hello. I'll do this and...

1140
01:00:15,738 --> 01:00:17,156
Yeah.

1141
01:00:23,579 --> 01:00:24,872
You have to answer.

1142
01:00:25,414 --> 01:00:26,623
[sighs]

1143
01:00:30,627 --> 01:00:31,837
[exhales]

1144
01:00:34,214 --> 01:00:36,050
This marriage isn't gonna work.

1145
01:00:36,759 --> 01:00:39,678
<i>♪ It's you, just us ♪</i>

1146
01:00:40,387 --> 01:00:41,971
<i>♪ Just this ♪</i>

1147
01:00:41,972 --> 01:00:43,306
<i>♪ Just 'cause ♪</i>

1148
01:00:43,307 --> 01:00:45,059
<i>♪ Just because ♪</i>

1149
01:00:46,393 --> 01:00:49,312
<i>♪ When you say my name, it's different ♪</i>

1150
01:00:49,313 --> 01:00:53,524
<i>♪ Just because ♪</i>

1151
01:00:53,525 --> 01:00:58,321
<i>♪ Every little second feels infinite ♪</i>

1152
01:00:58,322 --> 01:01:02,367
<i>♪ No lie, no reason ♪</i>

1153
01:01:02,368 --> 01:01:04,327
<i>♪ No fair design ♪</i>

1154
01:01:04,328 --> 01:01:06,829
<i>♪ I am yours ♪</i>

1155
01:01:06,830 --> 01:01:10,333
<i>♪ I'm yours ♪</i>

1156
01:01:10,334 --> 01:01:13,337
<i>♪ Just because ♪</i>

1157
01:01:14,046 --> 01:01:15,422
[Yi-ji] <i>Am I all right now?</i>

1158
01:01:16,340 --> 01:01:17,632
[Sun-woo] <i>You're the victim.</i>

1159
01:01:17,633 --> 01:01:20,009
[Byung-je] <i>The incident
has escalated too much.</i>

1160
01:01:20,010 --> 01:01:21,677
[Yi-ji] <i>If I were to give up now,</i>

1161
01:01:21,678 --> 01:01:24,223
it would feel as though the past ten years
of my life were wasted.

1162
01:01:25,099 --> 01:01:28,184
Still, if you can, give it everything
you've got. You can do it.

1163
01:01:28,185 --> 01:01:31,562
I want to learn how to do the job properly
under a capable boss.

1164
01:01:31,563 --> 01:01:33,815
- If you're not getting in, I'll go.
- I... I'm getting in. I'm getting in.

1165
01:01:33,816 --> 01:01:36,359
[Dong-seok] <i>Do you think
you have another option besides me?</i>

1166
01:01:36,360 --> 01:01:37,944
WE WILL NEVER FORGET
OUR LATE COLLEAGUE, KIM HYEON-I

1167
01:01:37,945 --> 01:01:39,904
[Yi-ji] <i>Could I love someone...</i>

1168
01:01:39,905 --> 01:01:41,614
[Sun-woo] <i>I can do it.</i>

1169
01:01:41,615 --> 01:01:44,367
[Yi-ji] <i>...and live with them
for the rest of my life?</i>

1170
01:01:44,368 --> 01:01:47,329
[theme song fades]
